ottages, small alleys, and craft and gift shops, climbing the slopes above Portminster harbour (facing east into the bay) and crossing the ridge to Portmeor beach (facing north into the Atlantic). These two coastlines meet at the headland called \"The Island\". South of the main town and railway station, St Ives straggles into Carbis Bay.","grounding":[{"source":"wikivoyage","title":"St Ives","url":"https://en.wikivoyage.org/wiki/St_Ives","licence":"CC BY-SA 4.0"}],"short":"Art and beaches share St Ives, a small Cornwall town on the United Kingdom coast. Tate St Ives and the Barbara Hepworth Museum and Sculpture Garden take up most of three hours, and the place fills between June and September.","short_src":"rewrite","facts":{"population":5410,"visit_h":2.5}},"highlights":[{"id":"hl-st-michael-s-mount","name":"St Michael's Mount","kind":"Island","lat":50.11694,"lon":-5.47797,"dist_km":10.1,"rank_score":9.88,"resolved_by":"catalogue"},{"id":"hl-tate-st-ives","name":"Tate St Ives","kind":"Museum","lat":50.21472,"lon":-5.48472,"dist_km":0.8,"rank_score":8.83,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/29/External_tate_st_ives.jpg/960px-External_tate_st_ives.jpg","author":"flickr user \"Steve Parker\"","licence":"CC BY 2.0","licence_url":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:External_tate_st_ives.jpg","w":1600,"h":1707,"ok_print":true}},{"id":"hl-47th-g7-summit","name":"47th G7 summit","kind":"Peak","lat":50.1982,"lon":-5.4666,"dist_km":1.5,"rank_score":7.7,"resolved_by":"catalogue","image":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a8/P20210611AS-0528_%2851269443335%29.jpg/960px-P20210611AS-0528_%2851269443335%29.jpg","author":"The White House","licence":"Public domain","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:P20210611AS-0528_(51269443335).jpg","w":3000,"h":2000,"ok_print":true}},{"id":"hl-men-an-tol","name":"Mên-an-Tol","kind":"Ruins